From 041f29fbeab9b66a97269b902bf7440dadaa51f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:07:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 36/41] [mpegts] Tell the end of a segment from the end of the
 stream

4875af2 sent an E-AC-3 frame alone at the end of the data when no byte
followed, and waited in every other case. Both rules were wrong:

- At a segment end exactly between the two frames of a 7.1 access unit,
  the seek scan sent the independent frame alone, and the dependent
  frame in the next segment had no frame before. With video, a seek to
  the key frame of the next segment returned that frame as a copy
  without the dependent frame (all 12 variants of the new 0-byte case).
- At the real end of the stream, a dependent frame or header that the
  stream cut made the parser wait for data that never came, and the
  independent frame before was lost.

GetEndPacket now takes endOfStream. The flush at a segment end
(ReadNextPacket with m_stopAtSegmentEnd) passes false, and the public
ReadEndPacket, which the sample reader calls only when no segment
follows, passes true. The E-AC-3 parser waits for the rest of an access
unit at a segment end, and sends the frame alone only at the end of the
stream. The video parsers keep es_end_of_data and flush at both ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
